    explanation: "- Prometheus scrapes a text exposition format over HTTP. Counters only increase, gauges move both ways, and histograms count observations into cumulative buckets with a mandatory +Inf bucket\n- Every unique label combination is a separate time series, so a label with unbounded values — a user id, a raw URL, a request id — multiplies series until the server falls over. Use the route template and the status class, not the path and the exact code\n- Histogram buckets are chosen up front and cannot be changed retroactively, so pick them around the latency you actually care about\n- OpenTelemetry propagates W3C trace context: traceparent carries version, trace id, span id and flags. Every service in a request shares the trace id and contributes its own span\n- Generating a new trace id when an inbound traceparent exists breaks the trace in half, and a caught error that is never recorded on the span leaves the trace looking healthy\n- Loki indexes labels, not log bodies. Keep labels low-cardinality and put the trace id in the JSON body, where it is searchable without being indexed\n- An SLO turns reliability into a number: the objective, the window, and the error budget that follows. Burn rate is how many times faster than sustainable the budget is being spent\n- Multi-window alerting is what prevents fatigue: page only when a fast burn in a short window is confirmed by a longer one, and raise a ticket for slow burns",
